      "dom_id": "question-11730",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=9{e}^{x}-9{x}^{2}+11x-20$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{x}-9{x}^{2}+11x-20) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(11x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(20) \\\\  & =9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+11\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-0 \\\\  & =9{e}^{x}-9(2x)+11(1) \\\\  & =9{e}^{x}-18x+11.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
